{"title":"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa9bc3e1ca566d171ec6b80e39ee4cc913b5aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> students at King Middle School are divided into three groups of equal size for lunch.  Each group has lunch at a different time.  A computer randomly assigns each student to one of three lunch groups.  The probability that three friends, Al, Bob, and Carol, will be assigned to the same lunch group is approximately\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10ee5d5081ab382ff6d7c7c3fedff911e506c9fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{27} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{9} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{8} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{6} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"362\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose Al, Bob and Carol are the first three students to be randomly assigned groups, in that order.  After Al is assigned to a group, his group has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f31ff033089cb9cfa5a6ce6cd9a0ce6b5c57422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$199$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> open seats, out of a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/63820cb161fab05852a3bc89a50cf90162dc9b43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$599$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> open seats across all the groups.  Therefore, the probability Bob is also assigned to this group is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/328025bfb1c209be18cc1a07eb0f6ca4eaa46b02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{199}{599}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />, which is slightly less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.  Similarly, if Al and Bob are assigned to the same group, the probability Carol is also assigned to this group is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e01dd8d7b8a226b84584d2c86cd6b173f5706660.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{198}{598}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />, which is also slightly less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.  So, the probability all three of them end up in the same group is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/6/0163642eb5ab650bf2fddd92fdf5c7851598b80b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{199}{599} \\cdot \\frac{198}{598}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"37\" />, which is slightly less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9e0646fe3f8c6f379b825d82aa2b97c27758b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\frac{1}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"118\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME\" title=\"1986 AJHSME\">1986 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1986\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME